<title>UK: UK'S MMS farms out Romania oil patch to Clyde.</title>
<headline>UK'S MMS farms out Romania oil patch to Clyde.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK independent oil explorer MMS Petroleum plc said it had agreed to farm out to Gulf Canada Resources subsidiary Clyde Petroleum a majority share of its exploration venture in Romania.</p>
<p>Clyde will earn 70 percent of the MMS interest in a production sharing agreement with state Petrom company covering block six in Romania's eastern Carpathian oil and gas producing region.</p>
<p>Clyde will reimburse MMS for some past work and carry the MMS share of the costs of technical work during the first period of the licence up to a maximum gross cost of $4 million.</p>
<p>The agreement is conditional on Romanian government approval.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
